1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,460
Hey, Toka, will you let me in?

2
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,400
Please, just hear me out.

3
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:10,900
Why don't you go talk to your little girlfriend?

4
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:14,260
I have nothing more to say about it, you dummy dum-dum-dum!

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:44,880
Rain, it's just like a girl, sometimes kind, sometimes fickle, pouring down heavily, or

6
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:48,880
not falling at all, it is the source of all life.

7
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:53,580
And tonight, the rain is a little cold.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:17,740
I will let you in!

9
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:23,480
The lights for the light

10
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:28,980
Is all Lydia JACOBE is certain

11
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:34,420
And every day, I've taken a mile

12
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:38,060
Look at my eyes till my dreams

13
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:44,800
This4844 miyago is insane

14
00:01:44,800 --> 00:02:14,780
See you next time.

15
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:18,800
I'll get right to the point here, Toka.

16
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,540
You've been really irritated lately.

17
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:23,860
Please just tell me what's going on.

18
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:28,140
Though if I had to take a wild guess, I'd say this is about Shido and that girl.

19
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:31,700
No. No, you're wrong. This has nothing to do with him.

20
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:34,380
Oh. I just assumed he was the cause of it.

21
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:41,380
I don't know what's wrong.

22
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:44,960
I'm in the worst mood ever, and I'm not even sure I know why.

23
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:57,400
Uh, Mio Shinon?

24
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:01,880
Wait, hold on a second. Don't run away.

25
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,140
Oh, hey, what happened to your puppet?

26
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:10,340
Oh, I see. That's what you're looking for?

27
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:15,240
Shido can do whatever he wants.

28
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:19,540
It's really none of my business who he dates or kisses or spends his free time with.

29
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:21,540
But when I saw that, it just...

30
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:24,100
I felt awful all of a sudden.

31
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:28,560
Then when I heard the rabbit say Shido cared more about that other girl than me,

32
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:31,060
it was like I was empty inside.

33
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:32,600
Like I was all alone.

34
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:36,460
Sad. That's what it made me feel more than anything else.

35
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:37,360
Scared, too.

36
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:40,700
I'm really worried there might be something wrong with me.

37
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:43,320
Gotcha.

38
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:47,220
So you lost it while you were fighting the AST yesterday?

39
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:50,760
Kotri, do you copy that?

40
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:52,920
Yeah, we're analyzing the video now.

41
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:56,280
You take the lead on the search, and we'll support you as much as we can.

42
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:58,140
But we're gonna take a back seat on this one.

43
00:03:58,580 --> 00:04:00,640
It'll be better if all her attention is on you.

44
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:04,660
Yoshinan, we're ready to start whenever you are.

45
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:08,020
See, the thing is, my name is...

46
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:09,180
It's not Yoshinan.

47
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:13,140
It's Yoshinan, and Yoshinan is the puppet we're looking for.

48
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:15,260
And my friend...

49
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:16,000
Yoshinan.

50
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:17,220
I gotcha.

51
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:19,920
Wait a sec.

52
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:23,500
Please, take it.

53
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,820
You could catch a bad cold in a rainstorm like this.

54
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:31,880
Oh, don't worry.

55
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:32,680
I'll be all right.

56
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:34,580
Really, I want you to have it.

57
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:41,140
Mom, that's very kind of you.

58
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:41,940
Sure.

59
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:44,600
There is absolutely nothing wrong with you.

60
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,260
But listen, I think we should definitely clear a few things up.

61
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:49,240
Like what?

62
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:52,320
Well, you should know that kiss was an accident.

63
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:53,140
Completely.

64
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:58,220
And it's not remotely true that Shido cares more about that other girl than he does about you.

65
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:01,180
Yes, but Shido was...

66
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:02,120
Just think about it.

67
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:03,660
He risked his life to save you.

68
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:08,080
Do you seriously believe he would have put himself in danger like that if he didn't care one bit?

69
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:09,700
Watch out!

70
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:19,400
Yoshinan?

71
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:20,500
Are you hungry?

72
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:29,740
Why don't you two take a break and get something to eat?

73
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:32,220
Might give you a chance to ask her some questions.

74
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:33,820
Yeah, good call.

75
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:37,380
But it looks like the fighting put these restaurants out of commission.

76
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:38,940
Let's go to my house.

77
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:39,920
We can eat there.

78
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:43,760
You sure love that puppet, don't you?

79
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:46,800
Most people would just give up and go buy a new one.

80
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:48,840
She must be really important to you, huh?

81
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:51,380
Oh, she is.

82
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:53,020
Yoshinan is my friend.

83
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:54,340
My best friend.

84
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:56,620
And she's my hero, too.

85
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,180
Your hero?

86
00:05:58,660 --> 00:05:59,440
Oh, yes.

87
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:02,060
See, Yoshinan is the greatest.

88
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:03,840
She's who I want to be.

89
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:05,260
She's just so brave.

90
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:06,600
So strong.

91
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:08,540
She's not pathetic like I am.

92
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:11,340
If I could be more like her, I would be so happy.

93
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:12,400
But I'm not.

94
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:13,520
And I'll never be.

95
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,920
Well, I don't know about all that.

96
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:19,100
But as a matter of fact, I like you just the way you are.

97
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:21,540
Hey.

98
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,040
Something wrong?

99
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:24,140
Oh, well.

100
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,940
No one's ever said that before.

101
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:27,320
Thank you.

102
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:28,420
It's nice.

103
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:31,700
Did you rehearse that line, or did it just come to you?

104
00:06:31,940 --> 00:06:34,740
Commander, here's the analysis of the puppet in the videos.

105
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:41,580
Yoshinan, why don't you ever try and fight back when the AST attacks you?

106
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,740
There's got to be a reason for it.

107
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:45,000
Yes, there is.

108
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:49,420
The thing is, I don't like pain, or being scared.

109
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:50,760
I can't stand it.

110
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:52,820
I bet everyone hates those things, though.

111
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:53,940
How could they not?

112
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:56,460
Any creature that feels has to despise them.

113
00:06:56,860 --> 00:06:57,800
Don't you think so?

114
00:06:58,080 --> 00:06:58,780
Yeah, maybe.

115
00:06:59,160 --> 00:06:59,820
One would hope.

116
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:02,160
Then again, I'm just a big scaredy cat.

117
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:04,480
When I'm scared, I freeze up.

118
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:07,720
I can't think, or move, or speak.

119
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:09,040
I'm so afraid.

120
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:11,060
It's like I can't do anything at all.

121
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:13,820
Except stand there, hoping someone will save me.

122
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:15,400
It's awful.

123
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:18,600
If I wasn't such a coward, I might be able to fight back.

124
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:20,820
But, I am.

125
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,160
Always have been.

126
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:24,440
The truth is, I'm nothing like Yoshinan.

127
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:27,520
When I'm in danger, she's right there by my side.

128
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:28,080
Always.

129
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:30,960
She gives me the courage I don't have on my own.

130
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:33,820
She's strong, brave, and fearless.

131
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:35,340
She's my hero.

132
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:37,460
So you see, that's it.

133
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:39,260
That's why I won't fight.

134
00:07:42,180 --> 00:07:43,740
Why are you petting me?

135
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:44,420
Come on.

136
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:46,120
I'm here to protect you.

137
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:49,700
And I'll make sure we find Yoshinan.

138
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:53,480
But, you don't have to rely on her to protect you anymore.

139
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:55,360
Because I'm going to be your hero now.

140
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:57,740
That's right.

141
00:07:58,240 --> 00:07:59,960
It doesn't matter if she's a spirit.

142
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:03,520
But, a girl as kind as she is, deserves nothing less.

143
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:05,840
Thanks so much for your kindness.

144
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:06,860
Sure.

145
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:10,720
So, look.

146
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,880
I'm sorry about what happened.

147
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:14,860
Kissing you out of the blue and everything.

148
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:16,100
Kissing?

149
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:16,660
Yeah.

150
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:17,340
You know.

151
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:21,360
A kiss is when you get really close and touch each other's lips.

152
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:22,580
Just like this.

153
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,720
Shido, I'm so sorry that I...

154
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:43,840
Shido, sorry to bother you at a time like this,

155
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:45,680
but we figured out where Yoshinan is.

156
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:46,640
Great.

157
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:47,520
Awesome work.

158
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:48,540
Tell me where.

159
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:51,280
Actually, that's kind of the awkward part.

160
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:58,480
There's that feeling again.

161
00:08:58,540 --> 00:08:59,240
It's awful.

162
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:01,320
I just wanted to go away.

163
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:09,700
Who's there?

164
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:10,540
It's Shido.

165
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:12,280
Can I come...

166
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:20,880
This is crazy.

167
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:23,560
Are you positive I'm in the right place?

168
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:26,060
According to the analysis, there's no question.

169
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:28,560
We were able to confirm beyond a shadow of a doubt

170
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:30,580
that Origami took Yoshinan from the scene.

171
00:09:30,940 --> 00:09:32,440
That doesn't make me feel any better

172
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,960
about having to act like a thief.

173
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:35,840
Well, it's too late to back out now.

174
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:37,780
We'll do our best to support you in order.

175
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,320
And if that could you happen...

176
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:39,540
Hello?

177
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:41,060
You there?

178
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:41,120
You there?

179
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:56,580
Hi there, Tobechi.

180
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:57,520
Hello.

181
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,120
Thanks for letting me come over.

182
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,020
I know it's really short notice and all.

183
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:06,120
I appreciate it.

184
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:07,180
You're very welcome.

185
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,420
Here you go.

186
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:12,000
Oh, uh, thank you.

187
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:14,400
Wait!

188
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:15,340
Tobechi!

189
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:16,260
What is this?

190
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:16,920
Just drink it.

191
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:17,700
Come on!

192
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:18,920
You gotta be kidding me!

193
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:19,660
Drink it.

194
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:22,000
Of course.

195
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:22,800
I would love to.

196
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:30,920
Hey, what in the heck do you think you're doing?

197
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,420
Do you like that?

198
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:35,060
Well, uh, I would say no.

199
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:36,080
Not really.

200
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:39,700
I'll get off you if you agree to grant me one request.

201
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,480
No ifs, ands, or buts.

202
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:42,820
Do we have a deal or not?

203
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:44,360
Depends on what it is.

204
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:47,420
I'm completely over you calling me by my last name.

205
00:10:47,780 --> 00:10:48,400
You got that?

206
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:50,800
I hear you call everybody else by their first names.

207
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:53,000
But I'm still just Tobechi to you.

208
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:53,620
Huh?

209
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:54,860
My name's Origami.

210
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,960
That is what I prefer to be called.

211
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:57,860
Deal?

212
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:00,720
That seems like a reasonable proposition.

213
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:02,120
Consider it done.

214
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:08,520
Yeah, Origami.

215
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:12,460
We good?

216
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:14,240
Uh, totally, sure.

217
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:18,520
Wait, where are you going?

218
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,480
The shower.

219
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:23,680
Seems like a weird time to do that.

220
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:24,980
Oh, I forgot!

221
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:25,680
The puppet!

222
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:51,240
Oh, yeah!

223
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:56,660
No use.

224
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:57,760
I can't find it.

225
00:11:57,980 --> 00:11:58,540
Damn it.

226
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:01,320
These not-so-subtle pillow messages are freaking me out.

227
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:14,480
Oh, wow.

228
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:15,300
That was pretty fast.

229
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:21,500
What's wrong?

230
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,240
Oh, nothing is wrong.

231
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:23,720
Why?

232
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:26,800
Are you okay?

233
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:28,780
Dude, how can you ask me that?

234
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:32,180
We still haven't been able to reestablish the connection?

235
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:33,240
No, not yet.

236
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:35,300
There's some sort of powerful jamming signal there.

237
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:37,620
And it's far stronger than the signal at AST.

238
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:38,980
Origami.

239
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:40,060
What is her deal?

240
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:42,040
There's something I want to ask you.

241
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:46,040
During one of my missions, I was sure you'd been...

242
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:48,840
I want to know what you are.

243
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:50,660
Look.

244
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,400
Have you ever talked to a spirit before?

245
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:55,080
What are you trying to say?

246
00:12:55,420 --> 00:12:56,880
I'm saying I've talked to them.

247
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,440
And not just Toka, either.

248
00:12:58,840 --> 00:12:59,840
I've talked with Yoshino.

249
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,720
She's the spirit they call the Hermit.

250
00:13:01,860 --> 00:13:02,940
That's too dangerous.

251
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:04,460
You shouldn't do that.

252
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:05,620
It's really not.

253
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:06,860
You should give it a try.

254
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:08,180
I think you'll be surprised.

255
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:09,820
Look, you're right.

256
00:13:09,880 --> 00:13:12,140
There probably are a ton of bad spirits out there.

257
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:13,720
But they're not all bad.

258
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:16,380
I know this might sound a little bit nuts.

259
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:17,720
But you gotta believe me.

260
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:18,160
It's true.

261
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:20,380
Toka and Yoshino are good spirits.

262
00:13:21,220 --> 00:13:22,680
I have to help Yoshino.

263
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:25,580
And no matter what, I'll never deny Toka.

264
00:13:26,220 --> 00:13:27,380
You asked something of me.

265
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:29,640
Now I'm gonna demand something of you.

266
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:31,040
Promise me something.

267
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:33,220
Promise you'll stop hurting good people.

268
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:35,440
You're a good person, too.

269
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:37,220
And they're no different than you are.

270
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:39,920
So tell me, why the hell did it have to turn out this way?

271
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:40,980
Look, I don't know.

272
00:13:41,220 --> 00:13:42,460
But it just can't be helped.

273
00:13:43,460 --> 00:13:45,240
Even if you are right about them,

274
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:47,700
and even if that Hermit isn't looking for a fight,

275
00:13:48,060 --> 00:13:50,180
there's still the problem of the Spatial Quakes.

276
00:13:51,980 --> 00:13:52,680
It's them.

277
00:13:53,220 --> 00:13:54,340
We're being deployed.

278
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:57,240
Origami, let me ask you one more thing.

279
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:00,720
If Hermit's spirit powers give out like Toka's did,

280
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:02,140
you'll stop attacking, won't you?

281
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:04,260
That would be the right thing to do.

282
00:14:04,900 --> 00:14:08,080
It isn't about being right or wrong, good or bad.

283
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,860
It's about following my orders,

284
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:12,100
regardless of whatever I might want to do.

285
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:13,460
All right, Origami.

286
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:14,260
Goodbye.

287
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:15,280
I'll see you soon.

288
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:32,440
Yes, we've got her right where we want her.

289
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:48,520
Did we get her?

290
00:14:58,900 --> 00:15:00,940
Bro, what is it?

291
00:15:00,940 --> 00:15:30,400
This can't be real.

292
00:15:30,940 --> 00:15:36,820
Move. Let's go.

293
00:15:41,820 --> 00:15:42,460
Yoshino!

294
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:46,160
It's me. I'm here.

295
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:48,040
He... he came.

296
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:51,480
Yoshino!

297
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:53,560
I came here to give you something.

298
00:15:53,560 --> 00:16:01,700
What do you think you're doing?

299
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,380
It's not safe over there.

300
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:06,620
No! No!

301
00:16:06,620 --> 00:16:14,680
Shino!

302
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:15,920
Oh, no.

303
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:17,420
This is not good.

304
00:16:17,420 --> 00:16:18,300
Sand upon!

305
00:16:18,300 --> 00:16:18,820
Sand upon!

306
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:20,020
Sand upon!

307
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:20,700
Sand upon!

308
00:16:21,860 --> 00:16:22,300
Why?

309
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:23,160
Please.

310
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:24,120
Sand upon!

311
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:25,960
Sand upon!

312
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:29,780
Sand upon!

313
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:37,380
Sand upon!

314
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:40,200
Sand upon!

315
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:40,620
Sand upon!

316
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:41,620
Sand upon!

317
00:16:42,260 --> 00:16:43,200
Sand upon!

318
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:43,860
Sand upon!

319
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:44,640
Sand upon!

320
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:45,400
Sand upon!

321
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:45,800
Sand upon!

322
00:16:45,860 --> 00:16:45,960
Sand upon!

323
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:47,040
Sand upon!

324
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:50,160
Oh, man. Sandalfon.

325
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:56,820
Are you okay?

326
00:16:57,860 --> 00:17:00,080
Toka? You saved me.

327
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:03,640
Oh, Shiro. I owe you an apology for lots of things.

328
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:06,640
I got mad at you about some stuff I didn't really know about.

329
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:09,020
I hope you can find it in your heart to forgive me.

330
00:17:09,380 --> 00:17:11,740
Thank you. But I'm the one who should apologize.

331
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:15,300
Toka, I need your power to save Yoshino.

332
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:22,920
Yoshino, she's the girl you kissed.

333
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:27,380
I see. She is more important to you than I am.

334
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:28,880
I understand.

335
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:31,700
No, that's not how it is at all.

336
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:36,320
Yoshino, she's... she's a spirit just like you.

337
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:42,020
I made a promise that I'd do everything I could to protect her,

338
00:17:42,220 --> 00:17:43,740
but I can't do it on my own.

339
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:46,640
I'm begging you. Please.

340
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:48,040
Lend me your power.

341
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:54,120
His heart is so... good.

342
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:56,540
How can I turn my back on him?

343
00:17:57,040 --> 00:17:58,260
The man who saved me.

344
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:00,300
I have to do the right thing.

345
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:03,000
Toka?

346
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:08,860
Get on. There's not much time.

347
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:13,440
This is definitely not a good sign.

348
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:17,120
It looks like the blizzard is taking the magical power from our realizers

349
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:18,980
and using it to strengthen its defenses.

350
00:18:19,780 --> 00:18:22,620
And there's no way we can lower the territory and go in there.

351
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:24,840
We won't be able to withstand the ice bullets.

352
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,540
They'll rip us all to shreds.

353
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:31,120
Besides, if we only use physical attacks, we won't be able to do anything about the spirit.

354
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:32,280
Origami.

355
00:18:32,280 --> 00:18:39,920
Wait, what is this?

356
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,080
What are you doing?

357
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:42,440
I'll use sheer force.

358
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:45,140
Attack at the exact moment the barrier falls.

359
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:57,940
Excellent dodge.

360
00:18:58,340 --> 00:18:59,600
Toka Yatogami.

361
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:05,740
Why don't you just give up while you still can?

362
00:19:05,740 --> 00:19:09,160
Troops, switch your target to princess.

363
00:19:22,820 --> 00:19:24,120
Shino, hold on.

364
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:26,000
Please don't go in there on your own.

365
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:29,580
With no protection, this is too much, even with your regeneration abilities.

366
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:30,660
Wait a sec.

367
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:34,400
Am I going crazy or do I detect just a hint of concern in your voice?

368
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:36,440
This is no time to joke around, Shino.

369
00:19:37,040 --> 00:19:38,780
Last time a single bullet hit you.

370
00:19:39,140 --> 00:19:41,440
Trust me, this is going to be a completely different story.

371
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:44,440
It'll be like trying to dodge machine gun fire.

372
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:47,840
If your spirit power is detected, you won't be able to heal.

373
00:19:48,180 --> 00:19:48,980
Spirit power?

374
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:50,040
Oh, wow.

375
00:19:50,340 --> 00:19:53,340
So my regeneration ability, it's a spirit power then?

376
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:56,940
Shino, don't do this.

377
00:19:56,940 --> 00:19:57,460
Please.

378
00:19:58,140 --> 00:19:59,600
Don't go in there, big bro.

379
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:02,720
Yoshino.

380
00:20:02,720 --> 00:20:04,520
Have no fear.

381
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:05,940
Yoshinan's here.

382
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:23,000
It's...

383
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:24,400
It's really you, Shino.

384
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:26,080
In the flesh.

385
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:28,900
I made it.

386
00:20:29,340 --> 00:20:30,600
Just in the nick of time.

387
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:32,520
Here's your puppet.

388
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:34,460
See, I told you I'd find it.

389
00:20:38,860 --> 00:20:40,040
No, what's wrong?

390
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:41,720
Hey, please don't cry.

391
00:20:41,980 --> 00:20:43,240
Everything is going to be alright.

392
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:43,980
Thank you.

393
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:46,400
You're just so nice.

394
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:49,560
Thanks for saving her.

395
00:20:49,820 --> 00:20:50,260
She...

396
00:20:50,260 --> 00:20:51,960
She's my best friend.

397
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:53,820
This means so much to me.

398
00:20:57,820 --> 00:20:58,980
Glad to do it.

399
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:00,900
But now it's your turn to be saved.

400
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:01,880
Huh?

401
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:03,960
But first, uh...

402
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:05,100
You see...

403
00:21:05,100 --> 00:21:07,980
The thing is, in order to save you, there's something we have to do.

404
00:21:08,460 --> 00:21:11,100
We have to kiss first, so...

405
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:15,580
Oh, uh...

406
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:16,760
Well, not really.

407
00:21:17,560 --> 00:21:18,720
I was just kidding around.

408
00:21:19,260 --> 00:21:21,520
We don't actually have to do that if you don't...

409
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:25,680
Was that okay with you?

410
00:21:26,300 --> 00:21:26,820
Yeah.

411
00:21:27,220 --> 00:21:28,320
Yeah, it was awesome.

412
00:21:28,820 --> 00:21:29,680
Sure was.

413
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:30,580
I'm glad.

414
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:33,540
Because if you think it's awesome, then it's awesome to meet, too.

415
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:39,240
Whoa!

416
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:40,480
What's happening?

417
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:42,080
Oshida!

418
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:42,280
Oh!

419
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:56,820
Yorah!

420
00:21:59,220 --> 00:22:04,040
Kami様どうか 教えてください

421
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:09,580
明日私はどこへ行くの?

422
00:22:10,340 --> 00:22:15,140
傷つくたびに 評価に変えた

423
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:20,640
心が熱を 出してる

424
00:22:21,520 --> 00:22:45,140
君はどうして微笑んでるの 何度も背中向けたのに 太陽が今燃え落ちたら この涙 雨に変えて抱きしめたい

425
00:22:45,140 --> 00:22:54,500
Hey, what the heck is this?

426
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:57,440
I told you we'd make a special housing unit just for spirits.

427
00:22:58,040 --> 00:22:59,560
Toka will move out today and live here.

428
00:22:59,840 --> 00:23:01,920
If you listened to me, you'd already know that.

429
00:23:02,560 --> 00:23:03,860
And not just Toka, either.

430
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:07,900
Uh, hi, Hoshino.

431
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:11,160
Hi. From now on, I'll be by your side.

432
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:14,160
Right. The same goes for me.

433
00:23:15,140 --> 00:23:24,320
This isn't the end, it's just the beginning, folks.

434
00:23:24,580 --> 00:23:25,640
To be continued.

435
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:27,380
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

